        "This is Missing not at random (MNAR). The reason for the lack of data is because patients with a lower socioeconomic status can't afford data plans for continous telemetry streaming. So it is systematic with income not random. Mean imputation would destroy integrity as it will replace all the missing values with the average heart rate across the data. But the missing valus belong specifically to the lower income patients filling that gap would misrepresent that subgroup."
